# The ClusterFuzzLite image derives from gcr.io/oss-fuzz-base/base-builder, which
# builds as root by design - the OSS-Fuzz tooling writes to $SRC and $OUT as root
# and ClusterFuzzLite drives it that way. Adding a USER line breaks the build,
# and the image never runs as a service.
# The CI image (.github/docker/ci.Dockerfile) is the same case: a GitHub Actions
# job container writes the workspace under /__w as root before any step runs, so
# a non-root USER breaks actions/checkout.
DS-0002
# HEALTHCHECK belongs to long-running service images. This one exists to compile
# fuzz targets and exits, and the CI image runs a build and exits the same way.
DS-0026
